task:
Add a read-only public ratings smoke check with a committed receipt (2026-10-31 audit leftover).

After each governed release the owner wants proof that Ratings V4 answers correctly on the public site, saved in the repository. Add scripts/checks/ratings_v4_public_smoke.py (CPython 3.14, standard library only, read-only HTTPS GETs, bounded timeouts, no credentials) that, against a base URL argument defaulting to https://ed-finder.app:
- GET /api/health and record build_sha and database status;
- GET /api/ratings/v4/generation (or the current generation route in apps/api/src/routers/ratings_v4.py) and record the generation id and scorer version;
- for a fixed list of three systems (Sol 10477373803 plus two others you choose that exist in the published generation, documented in the script), GET the system ratings and its explanation route, validate the response shapes against the Pydantic models' required fields (seven economies, 0–100 potentials, confidence 0–1, matching generation id), and time each request;
- write a JSON receipt (schema_version, base_url, started_at, build_sha, generation, per-request status/latency/validation result, overall status) to a path argument, and exit non-zero on any failure.
Document it in docs/operations/v3-production-application-release.md as a post-promotion step: run it, then commit the receipt under docs/operations/evidence/<date>-v3-ratings-v4-public-smoke-<build>.json in the release record PR. Unit tests with a local stub HTTP server (no network): pass case, wrong generation, out-of-range score, non-200, timeout. Add the script to any static script inventory tests that require it. CHANGES.md entry. Do not call production from tests or CI.
